{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1494394-random-ideas-for-pantheons","id":1494394,"title":"Random Ideas for Pantheons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-05T00:09:10-07:00","id":1494394,"title":"Random Ideas for Pantheons","content":"Just a few ideas<br /> <br /> A Machine Pantheon<br /> <br /> The main idea with this was to create a pantheon similar to the rithm from the dc universe. &quot;Born&quot; from a simulation Skaft had running in one of her labs the first members of this pantheon would manage to escape from the &quot;server&quot; they were held on and capture the &quot;mainframe&quot; of some long forgotten Atlantean facility outside of the city. There they would build themselves physical Avatars using Teros tech and sit out the fall of Atlantis. The Motif of the Pantheon would be the same as the Motif of the Teros and their virtues would be perfection and humanity. As Pantheon Purview i thought about something Cyberspace related but not sure what would really fit.<br /> <br /> A Pantheon for the unclaimed dead<br /> <br /> The world of Scion has quite the number of afterlifes. But what happens to those Souls which for whatever reason fall through the cracks of the system? Well according to me they end up on the barren plain a long since abandoned Afterlife from a long forgotten Pantheon. That is until a group of hopeful Demigods ended up their in search for an important Soul that had gone astray. Now stuck they feared to expire before reaching apotheosis but in a stroke of Genius (or Madness) managed to gain the worpship of all those lost souls by founding 5 pseudo-afterlifes upon the barren plain becoming gods. Now known collectively as the Ashen court the 5 new gods exist in a constant struggle for territory and souls fearing that a loss of said territory could cost them their godhood. This craven and somewhat selfish attitude is highlighted by their titan callings (mostly Tyrant but Advesary and monster are also likely).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T00:24:23-07:00","id":1494396,"title":"","content":"Before you go further on the \u201cMachine Pantheon\u201d, you might want to look at <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/321122\" target=\"_blank\">the New Gods</a> Nexus product: basically, a \u201cPantheon\u201d patterned loosely off of the new Gods in Neil Gaiman's <i>American Gods</i>. <br /> <br /> And the fate of unclaimed should of the dead is addressed in <b>Scion: Demigod</b>. It's actually somewhat similar to your starting point: they have their own Afterlife, which <i>isn't</i> government by any one Pantheon \u2014 but rather, is tended by a collection of gods from the various Pantheons working together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T01:30:55-07:00","id":1494399,"title":"","content":"Since there are hints that some pantheons came together as groups of Scions seeking to be the gods of a different group of people then it makes sense that if a new group is defined or otherwise comes into being a pantheon will form for them. To an extent, this is what the Loa are. <br /> <br /> I could see a group of Native American deities banding together with the idea that the surviving Native American groups constitute a new people that must act as a new super tribe in order to survive as a people and a culture. They would of course have complex relationships with the older pantheons. <br /> <br /> I could see several different groups trying to be the American pantheon. <br /> <br /> Some pantheons are wildly out of step with what their cultures have become. The Irish pantheon is a good example. I could see a new group of Scions trying to found a pantheon more suited to modern Ireland. As in the American example, there will be complications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-26T03:45:51-07:00","id":1495616,"title":"","content":"For the American pantheon i totally could see figures like Paul Bunyan and John Henry stepping in maybe even that wolf from &quot;where the water tastes like wine&quot; as a sort of carry over from one of the Native American Pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-26T12:04:38-07:00","id":1495630,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea. Certain traditions of high magic seek apotheosis as a goal. They believe every mortal has a spark of divinity within them that they can nurture and achieve godhood. <br /> <br /> Why not a group of magicians seeking apotheosis. A pantheon of self initiated gods. Each is their own divine parent and primordial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-26T17:22:33-07:00","id":1495639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1494394-random-ideas-for-pantheons?p=1495630#post1495630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an idea. Certain traditions of high magic seek apotheosis as a goal. They believe every mortal has a spark of divinity within them that they can nurture and achieve godhood.<br /> <br /> Why not a group of magicians seeking apotheosis. A pantheon of self initiated gods. Each is their own divine parent and primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> Sounds a lot like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1452937-cod-monsters-in-scion?p=1452956#post1452956\">how would you put <b>Mage: The Awakening</b> mages in <b>Scion</b> setting</a>. ( Or at least, Silver Ladder from it. \ud83d\ude0e )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-26T21:05:44-07:00","id":1495644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1494394-random-ideas-for-pantheons?p=1495630#post1495630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an idea. Certain traditions of high magic seek apotheosis as a goal. They believe every mortal has a spark of divinity within them that they can nurture and achieve godhood.<br /> <br /> Why not a group of magicians seeking apotheosis. A pantheon of self initiated gods. Each is their own divine parent and primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even better if their main source of Legend among the whole group is Invocation, and they attempt to uplift themselves as Gods in order to play-act as their own divine selves. Or if their main source is through Talismans, and they try to figure out a way to combine the powers of these disparate relics in order to create a basis for a Pantheon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-27T03:34:01-07:00","id":1495648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1494394-random-ideas-for-pantheons?p=1495644#post1495644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even better if their main source of Legend among the whole group is Invocation, and they attempt to uplift themselves as Gods in order to play-act as their own divine selves. Or if their main source is through Talismans, and they try to figure out a way to combine the powers of these disparate relics in order to create a basis for a Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some present day occultists think that's what Shakespeare and the other major Elizabethan and Jacobean dramatists were trying to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-27T03:34:50-07:00","id":1495649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1494394-random-ideas-for-pantheons?p=1495639#post1495639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Sounds a lot like <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1452937-cod-monsters-in-scion?p=1452956#post1452956&amp;quot;]how</a> would you put <b>Mage: The Awakening</b> mages in <b>Scion</b> setting[/URL]. ( Or at least, Silver Ladder from it. \ud83d\ude0e )</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage the Ascension please. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-27T13:35:01-07:00","id":1495678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1494394-random-ideas-for-pantheons?p=1495630#post1495630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an idea. Certain traditions of high magic seek apotheosis as a goal. They believe every mortal has a spark of divinity within them that they can nurture and achieve godhood.<br /> <br /> Why not a group of magicians seeking apotheosis. A pantheon of self initiated gods. Each is their own divine parent and primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds amazing although i am not sure if someone can be both god and Primordial. The new Scion: God manuscripts make them out to be quite different.<br /> <br /> But using the Avatar from MTA should make this a none issue. Since the Avatar can be the God but still be part of the greater Primordial. As virtues someone could take something like enlightment vs temptation. With enlightment representing forgoing his own desires in order to reach a higher state of being and temption the lure of using ones power for something that doesnt serve the idea of enlightment.<br /> <br /> I am currently making a Pantheon for Denizens with figures like R\u00fcbezahl and maybe Oberon as members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26520,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","user":"Mugbearer23","date":". 10-27-2022, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}